{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 133, :comments ["<b>My steps</b> — Let him pray to rectify his deeds, that he may keep positive commandments, and that causes leading him to commit negative commandments shall not gain dominion over him. And Rabbi Moses said: 'Let no iniquity gain dominion over me,' like 'and I am prayer' [Psalm 109:4]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "Resolved 'רבי משה' as Rabbi Moses [Ibn Chiquitilla] by inference from Ibn Ezra's standard citation practice."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:50.355792485Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}